---
id: air-grilled-rainbow-trout
title: Roasted Rainbow Trout
category: modular_protein

yield:
  servings: 1
  cooked_g: 195

storage:
  fridge_days: 2
  freezer_friendly: true

---

Pat @rainbow-trout-fillet{1} completely dry on both sides with paper towels, especially the skin.

Lightly brush the skin side with @avocado-oil{1/2%tsp} to keep it from sticking to the mesh. Season the flesh side evenly with @kosher-salt{1/4%tsp}, @black-pepper{1/4%tsp}, @garlic-powder{1/4%tsp}, and @smoked-paprika{1/4%tsp}.

Set the #oven to convection 200°C (400°F) and let it preheat fully, about 10 to 15 minutes. Place the seasoned fillet skin-side down on the mesh basket of the #crisper-tray; don't flip it. Roast on the middle rack for ~bake-time{8%min}, checking from the 7-minute mark.

Pull the fillet when internal temperature reaches 55°C to 57°C (130°F–135°F) at the thickest part checked with a #meat-thermometer (the flesh should be opaque and flake under gentle fork pressure; do not exceed 60°C/140°F to prevent moisture loss and albumin curds).

Let rest for ~rest-time{2%min}, then transfer the fillet (195 g cooked) into a meal prep container.
